What are CNG Vehicles?

CNG Vehicles are alternative fuel vehicles that use compressed natural gas instead of conventional gasoline or diesel. CNG is stored in high-pressure cylinders typically rated between 3,000 and 3,600 pounds per square inch (21 to 25 MPa). The vehicle's emissions profile is notably cleaner than traditional fuel vehicles, with substantially reduced carbon emissions and lower particulate matter per equivalent distance traveled. These vehicles typically demonstrate less wasted fuel and offer significant operational cost savings for both commercial fleet operators and individual consumers.

